course: dictionary
lesson: 7408
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the context: the words around it give clues. «The pointer on the dial moved to five.» A pointer here is the thin arrow or needle that points at a number, because a dial has a needle.
explain: «Can you give me some pointers?» Here pointers means useful tips or advice. Ask yourself: would a stick fit here? No, so it must mean tips. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: «The two end stars of the Plough's bowl, the Pointers, lead to Polaris, the Pole Star, which stays almost still above due north.» The capital P shows a name, and the stars point the way, so here the Pointers are two stars. Context is the key to choosing the right meaning.
fact: A pointer is a stick, arrow or needle used to point at something, such as on a dial, scale or clock.
fact: «Pointers» can mean useful tips or advice, as in «Can you give me some pointers?»
fact: On a computer, the pointer is the arrow you move with the mouse.
fact: A pointer is also a type of hunting dog.
fact: «The Pointers» are two stars in the Plough that lead to «Polaris», the Pole Star, which stays almost still above due north.
exercise: «The pointer on the dial moved to five.» What is the pointer? | A bowl for soup | *A stick, arrow or needle that points at something | A tip for doing better | A dog that hunts birds
exercise: «Can you give me some pointers?» What does pointers mean here? | Sharp sticks for hitting | *Useful tips or advice | Stars in the sky | Arrows on a computer screen
exercise: Which pointer do you move with a mouse? | A needle on a scale | A hunting dog | A star in the Plough | *The arrow on a computer screen
test: «The two end stars of the Plough's bowl, the Pointers, lead to Polaris.» In this sentence, what are the Pointers? | Needles on a dial | Useful tips | *Two stars that point towards Polaris | A type of dog
test: A pointer can be a type of what? | *A hunting dog | A bowl | A computer screen | A tip for cooking
exam: In «a laser pointer», which meaning of pointer fits best? | *A stick or light used to point at something | A hunting dog | A useful tip | A star in the sky
